{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Cat Stevens and Peter, Paul and Mary feel like natural next choices because their acoustic songwriting and vocal harmonies connect closely to my interest in Jonathan Edwards, Melanie, and Simon & Garfunkel.",
    "Fleetwood Mac and Eagles fit my interest in familiar, melodic classic rock, while the greatest hits format matches the collections I have repeatedly chosen."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Watermark feels less connected to the folk songs and classic rock collections I want to hear right now.",
    "Adele 21 connects to my occasional interest in newer pop, but that connection matters less today than the older songs and acoustic sound reflected in many of my choices."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A greatest hits title alone does not make a collection equally appealing; the voices, songwriting, and sound still determine which one I choose.",
    "My interest in some pop albums seems to have been treated as a stronger guide to my current mood than it is."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection among Jonathan Edwards, Melanie, and Simon & Garfunkel matters especially strongly to me when choosing acoustic songs and close vocal harmonies.",
    "I can enjoy Elvis, ABBA, Moody Blues, and Huey Lewis without choosing them today; with only a few selections, I favor the folk collections and melodic classic rock that most closely fit my mood."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in older hits collections, but only some captured the acoustic songwriting, harmonies, and melodic classic rock I most want today."
}"}
